  "reasoning": "The payer denied the claim with CO-22 (Coordination of Benefits), asserting another payer is primary, but the case facts confirm no secondary payer exists and the COB order is correct. Since the denial is based on a factual error regarding payer hierarchy rather than medical necessity or coding, a formal appeal is the appropriate mechanism to challenge the denial and provide evidence of the patient's single-payer status. The previous appeal attempt likely failed because it focused on medical necessity (CPT/diagnosis validity) rather than the specific CO-22 coordination issue, so this appeal must specifically address the absence of a primary payer.",
